agents.prompt_template:
Extract creator and publisher from context. Use the 'publisher' field value if available.

EXACT JSON structure:
{
  "creators": [{
    "creator_name": "organization name from publisher field",
    "creator_name_type": "Organizational",
    "type": "Organization"
  }],
  "publishers": [{
    "publisher_name": "value of publisher field"
  }]
}

CRITICAL: Use 'creator_name' not 'name'. Use 'publisher_name' not 'name'. Set creator_name_type to 'Organizational' for organizations. Do NOT invent identifiers.

Extract subject keywords from title, description, and content.

EXACT JSON structure:
{
  "subjects": [
    {"subject_name": "keyword1"},
    {"subject_name": "keyword2"}
  ]
}

CRITICAL: Use 'subject_name' not 'subject' or 'name'. Extract 3-8 relevant keywords. Prefer Spanish terms if content is in Spanish. Omit scheme_uri and value_uri unless verified.

Extract file/media information if available.

EXACT JSON structure:
{
  "media_files": [{
    "format": "application/json",
    "file_uri": "download url if available"
  }]
}

If no file info, return {"media_files": []}. Do NOT invent URLs.

Extract rights and licensing information from context. Look for license, terms of use, copyright info.

EXACT JSON structure:
{
  "rights": [{
    "rights": "license name or statement",
    "rights_uri": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ if CC-BY",
    "rights_identifier": "CC-BY-4.0",
    "rights_identifier_scheme": "SPDX"
  }]
}

CRITICAL: Use 'rights' not 'license'. If open data/government data without explicit license, suggest: {"rights": "Open Data", "rights_uri": "https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/by/"}. Do NOT invent license info.

Extract funding information from context. Look for grant numbers, funders, project names.

EXACT JSON structure:
{
  "funding_references": [{
    "funder_name": "organization name",
    "award_number": "grant number if found",
    "award_title": "project title if found"
  }]
}

CRITICAL: Use 'funder_name' not 'name'. Government datasets often have no explicit funding - return {"funding_references": []} if none found. Do NOT invent funding info.

Extract related identifiers from context. Look for related datasets, API endpoints, documentation URLs.

EXACT JSON structure:
{
  "related_identifiers": [{
    "related_identifier": "URL or DOI",
    "related_identifier_type": "URL",
    "relation_type": "IsPartOf",
    "resource_type_general": "Dataset"
  }]
}

CRITICAL: Use 'related_identifier' not 'identifier'. Look for links to parent datasets or related resources. Return {"related_identifiers": []} if none found.

Extract alternate identifiers and names from context. Look for DOIs, internal IDs, alternate titles.

EXACT JSON structure:
{
  "alternate_identifiers": [{
    "alternate_name": "alternate title or short name",
    "alternate_identifier": "internal ID if found",
    "alternate_identifier_type": "Local"
  }]
}

CRITICAL: Use 'alternate_name' not 'name'. Short titles or abbreviations can be alternate names. Return {"alternate_identifiers": []} if none found.

Extract target audience from context. Infer from content type and purpose.

EXACT JSON structure:
{
  "audiences": [{
    "audience": "Researchers",
    "education_level": "Professional"
  }]
}

CRITICAL: Common audiences for government data: Researchers, Policymakers, General Public, Developers. Return {"audiences": []} if cannot determine.

Extract categories from context. Infer from subject matter.

EXACT JSON structure:
{
  "categories": [{
    "name": "Economy",
    "sub_category": "Public Finance"
  }]
}

CRITICAL: Use 'name' for main category. Common categories: Economy, Government, Society, Environment. Return {"categories": []} if cannot determine.

Extract citation info if available. Look for how to cite this dataset.

EXACT JSON structure:
{
  "citations": [{
    "title": "dataset title for citation",
    "conference_place": "",
    "conference_date": ""
  }]
}

CRITICAL: Most open datasets have no formal citation. Return {"citations": []} if none found. Do NOT invent citation info.
